<title>MEXICO: Bufete wins BASF contract.</title>
<headline>Bufete wins BASF contract.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-04-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexican construction firm Bufete Industrial SA said on Saturday it has been awarded an engineering and procurement project by BASF Mexicana SA de CV.</p>
<p>BASF Mexicana is a wholly owned subsidiary of German-based chemical giant BASF AG. No value was given for the contract.</p>
<p>The project, which is scheduled to be completed by December, involves detailed engineering and procurement for a plant making ABS, a material needed for the automotive and electronic industries, Bufete said in a statement.</p>
<p>The plant, which will be located in Altamira, in Tamaulipas state in northern Mexico, is designed to produce 130,000 tons of ABS per year, Bufete said.</p>
<p>-- Dan Trotta, Mexico City bureau, +525 728-9507</p>
